Most of the contamination from photon conversion can be removed by applying this cut. The effect of this \(\delta\)-\(DipAngle\) cut on the \(\phi\) meson reconstruction efficiency is found to be small, lowering the efficiency by \(<5\%\) at \(p_{t}<1.0\) GeV/cand \(\sim\) 10% at \(p_{t}>\) 2.0 GeV/c.

