#### Nuclear modification factors

Nuclear modification factors are defined by

\[R_{AA}(p_{t})=\frac{[(d^{2}N/dp_{t})/N_{bin}]^{AA}}{[(\sigma_{NSD}/\sigma_{inel })d^{2}N/dp_{t}]^{NN}} \tag{3.3}\]

and

\[R_{CP}(p_{t})=\frac{[(d^{2}N/dp_{t})/N_{bin}]^{Central}}{[(d^{2}N/dp_{t})/N_{bin} ]^{Peripheral}}, \tag{3.4}\]

where \(R_{AA}\) is the yield ratio of \(A+A\) collisions to inelastic \(N+N\) collisions and \(R_{CP}\) is the yield ratio of central \(A+A\) collisions to peripheral \(A+A\) collisions,

\begin{table}
\begin{tabular}{l} \hline \hline Hijing events with \(\phi\) \\ \hline At least one \(\phi\) in \(|y|<\)0.5 \\ Daughter track \(K^{+}K^{-}\) flag \(>\) 0 \\ Daughter track \(K^{+}K^{-}\)\(|\eta|<\) 1.0 \\ Daughter track \(K^{+}K^{-}\) nFit \(\geq\) 15 \\ Daughter track \(K^{+}K^{-}\) nFit / nMax \(>\) 0.55 \\ \hline \hline \end{tabular}
\end{table}
