It has been found that strong auto-correlations exist when tracks used to calculate \(\phi\) invariant mass are also used to calculate the reaction plane angle. These auto-correlations are eliminated by excluding those tracks that are used for the \(\phi\) invariant mass calculation from the reaction plane angle estimation.

In order to calculate the observed \(v_{2}^{obs}\), the \(\phi\) meson yield is extracted in each \((p_{t},\varphi-\Psi_{2})\) bin. The extracted yield distribution as a function of \(\varphi-\Psi_{2}\) is then fitted by function

\[A[1+2v_{2}^{obs}\cos 2(\varphi-\Psi_{2})], \tag{3.8}\]

